      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HEZA PUNK ROCKER NZ (12) has won his past two, most recently scoring by 3.5 metres at Albion Park, and arrives in excellent form. The powerful Grimson stable has him back home, and even from a wide gate, he is expected to try for the front again, so stick with him. The hat-trick beckons. I GOT CHILLS NZ (7) is a stablemate of the top pick who also arrives off a strong win here over 1609m after placing the start before. A smart early drive could see him secure a trialling run, and from there, he would be hard to beat. VINCENZO (10) was solid when third here last week and is racing consistently enough to be a genuine top 3 threat again. NUGGET ROGERS (4) finished fourth last start when showing speed to lead here 11 days ago in lesser company, before fading late. This is tougher, but he can scrape into the top 4 with some luck. GO WITHOUT (2) gets his best draw in a while, and his last 2 starts at this level have been sound. Stick with him.",
